WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.447
Wednesday afternoon,
Orimere sends one line:

2
00:00:03.487 --> 00:00:07.075
9 Orchard Road moves to June 18.

3
00:00:07.115 --> 00:00:10.828
It lands in a shared inbox,
among two dozen hearings.

4
00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:14.715
Miss it,
and nobody shows up on the new day.

5
00:00:14.755 --> 00:00:17.930
In some offices,
the appeal can then be dismissed.

6
00:00:20.014 --> 00:00:22.345
Hearing Desk is built to catch it.

7
00:00:22.385 --> 00:00:27.534
The promise: every hearing,
a named yes, three working days ahead.

8
00:00:27.574 --> 00:00:33.381
People make every judgment call;
a fixed rule files only a plain yes.

9
00:00:33.421 --> 00:00:37.392
You'll see two layers:
this season's week-one kit,

10
00:00:37.432 --> 00:00:40.844
and a control tower built only if it pays.

11
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.045
Let's spend a day at the desk:
Friday, June 7,

12
00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:52.830
with 24 hearings this
week across 10 counties.

13
00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:57.640
Today shows only what needs you:
ten hearings at risk,

14
00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.414
and four close ones with no yes yet.

15
00:01:01.454 --> 00:01:03.550
We start with the mail.

16
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.227
Proposals wait here for a person.

17
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:10.732
Six new messages came in, and two AI
readers go through the new ones:

18
00:01:10.772 --> 00:01:13.687
one says what each proves,
the other checks it.

19
00:01:13.727 --> 00:01:16.254
The badge says live or recorded;

20
00:01:16.294 --> 00:01:19.017
a live read
takes 7 to 10 seconds a message,

21
00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:21.108
measured, so we trim the wait.

22
00:01:21.148 --> 00:01:23.197
Anything unclear goes to a person.

23
00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.514
Step one of the 9:00 a.m. pass.

24
00:01:26.554 --> 00:01:29.308
Nothing files itself: on unseen mail,

25
00:01:29.348 --> 00:01:33.258
about one agreed reading in ten was
still wrong in our measurements.

26
00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:35.250
So a person decides.

27
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:38.983
Velloran's email confirms
the date for 63 Garden Street.

28
00:01:39.023 --> 00:01:41.980
You accept,
and the desk shows where the link goes.

29
00:01:44.273 --> 00:01:46.888
Back to 9 Orchard Road.

30
00:01:46.928 --> 00:01:49.060
The firm planned this
move with the office:

31
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.654
Nora could cover both hearings
on the 18th, so we asked.

32
00:01:52.694 --> 00:01:55.479
Orimere moved one and kept the other.

33
00:01:55.519 --> 00:01:58.528
Only the office's written
word can close the date check,

34
00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:01.343
so you accept it,
and the desk lists what follows.

35
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.380
Each office has its own rules,
so each is a row of settings:

36
00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.869
how to tell it who's coming,
how far ahead, what proof it accepts.

37
00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:15.136
Where an office lets us plan dates,

38
00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:17.719
we ask for the days
our consultants promised;

39
00:02:17.759 --> 00:02:19.530
Larkmere hasn't answered yet.

40
00:02:20.457 --> 00:02:22.503
Tesswick changed its process by phone.

41
00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:23.777
A call isn't proof,

42
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:26.977
so its notices wait until
Alice approves the change,

43
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:28.657
with her name on it.

44
00:02:28.697 --> 00:02:30.487
She can always undo it.

45
00:02:32.716 --> 00:02:36.772
When a clerk writes back,
the office rule reads the reply.

46
00:02:36.812 --> 00:02:39.352
Tesswick's clerk can't find our form.

47
00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.236
That doesn't put our name on their record,

48
00:02:41.276 --> 00:02:45.746
so the check stays open,
and a call goes on today's list.

49
00:02:47.198 --> 00:02:51.318
To jump to any hearing,
press Control K and type the street.

50
00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:53.416
Here's a name check that's closed.

51
00:02:53.456 --> 00:02:55.318
Larkmere's clerk wrote back:

52
00:02:55.358 --> 00:02:57.998
staffing notices naming
Leo have been accepted.

53
00:02:58.038 --> 00:03:00.248
That written line is the proof.

54
00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.956
Now the consultants.

55
00:03:01.996 --> 00:03:05.689
They run their own businesses;
some keep no digital calendar.

56
00:03:05.729 --> 00:03:10.748
Maya gets one page from a link:
her week, where to be, what to bring.

57
00:03:10.788 --> 00:03:15.200
Her day-before message comes by email,
and she answers with one tap.

58
00:03:16.847 --> 00:03:20.167
Others would rather not share
their calendars, and they don't have to.

59
00:03:20.207 --> 00:03:21.809
The desk never looks at theirs;

60
00:03:21.849 --> 00:03:25.567
it hands them ours,
one file with 17 hearings.

61
00:03:25.607 --> 00:03:27.917
Editing that copy moves no hearing.

62
00:03:28.821 --> 00:03:32.201
Who to ask starts on the bench:
counties, daily caps,

63
00:03:32.241 --> 00:03:35.347
and what each consultant
told us about their days.

64
00:03:35.387 --> 00:03:38.421
Hearings come in groups,
one office, one day,

65
00:03:38.461 --> 00:03:41.298
so the whole docket goes
in one numbered text.

66
00:03:41.853 --> 00:03:44.242
When the offer was hearings one and three,

67
00:03:44.282 --> 00:03:48.457
YES 1 3 takes both,
and the reply rule files it.

68
00:03:48.497 --> 00:03:50.148
Take only part of a whole docket,

69
00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:52.639
like Leo here, and it goes to a person.

70
00:03:52.679 --> 00:03:56.964
So does anything unclear:
22 of 39 replies in our tests.

71
00:03:58.816 --> 00:04:00.313
Case files go out by version.

72
00:04:00.353 --> 00:04:03.161
Eli taps to say he has version 2.

73
00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:05.356
The files check closes only when the clerk

74
00:04:05.396 --> 00:04:08.066
and the consultant both
hold the current one.

75
00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:10.846
Some hearings end in an agreement.

76
00:04:10.886 --> 00:04:13.486
Priya's settlement for 16 Birch Lane needs

77
00:04:13.526 --> 00:04:16.206
her signature before
the hearing can close.

78
00:04:16.246 --> 00:04:18.106
She signs on her page.

79
00:04:18.146 --> 00:04:22.016
It's simulated here; at the firm,
it's their e-signature tool.

80
00:04:22.633 --> 00:04:24.346
Then a cancellation.

81
00:04:24.386 --> 00:04:28.855
Nora is ill and can't
make 34 Maple Lane on June 14.

82
00:04:28.895 --> 00:04:31.573
She taps Can't make it, picks the reason,

83
00:04:31.613 --> 00:04:34.543
and the coordinator has it days ahead,
not on the day.

84
00:04:36.573 --> 00:04:39.846
You accept,
and the desk says what to change:

85
00:04:39.886 --> 00:04:41.633
mark Nora unavailable that day,

86
00:04:41.673 --> 00:04:44.462
and offer the hearing
to the next consultant.

87
00:04:44.502 --> 00:04:45.979
Once someone says yes,

88
00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:49.263
the files and the office
notice start over for them.

89
00:04:49.417 --> 00:04:52.532
At 2 o'clock, the second pass:

90
00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:58.007
every flagged hearing gets a next step,
an owner and a time.

91
00:04:58.047 --> 00:05:03.844
Top of the list, 57 Clover Road:
the office asked twice for a statement,

92
00:05:03.884 --> 00:05:07.487
due at 4, and the coordinator
on duty owns it.

93
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:12.284
A hearing is covered by proof,
not feel: five of them.

94
00:05:12.324 --> 00:05:13.699
The office's date.

95
00:05:13.739 --> 00:05:15.460
The consultant's yes.

96
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:19.011
Our name on the office's record.
The files.

97
00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.741
And anything still owed.

98
00:05:20.781 --> 00:05:25.683
Until all five are in, or not needed,
it isn't ready.

99
00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:28.273
This morning, that's two of nineteen.

100
00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.608
Now jump ahead to the layer
that isn't built:

101
00:05:31.648 --> 00:05:36.071
the planned control tower,
where routine steps run themselves.

102
00:05:36.111 --> 00:05:40.837
A different case:
Leo can do 102 Willow Lane on June 10,

103
00:05:40.877 --> 00:05:43.544
but not 118 Willow Lane.

104
00:05:43.584 --> 00:05:46.780
The tower offers that one to Maya,
next on the list.

105
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.047
Play the queue forward
as if everyone says yes.

106
00:05:51.087 --> 00:05:53.857
Maya accepts, the current files follow,

107
00:05:53.897 --> 00:05:56.050
and the Larkmere office records her name.

108
00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:03.799
On the board, 118 Willow Lane
is ready again, with Maya attending.

109
00:06:03.839 --> 00:06:06.201
Every check is done or not needed,

110
00:06:06.241 --> 00:06:08.663
each proven by the party
that can prove it:

111
00:06:08.703 --> 00:06:12.460
Maya's yes, her files receipt,
and Larkmere's record.

112
00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:17.809
In code,
only the government moves a hearing date.

113
00:06:17.849 --> 00:06:19.110
Edit a shared calendar,

114
00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.450
and it's noted as what someone believes,
but the date stays.

115
00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:28.040
When the office moves it in writing,
the date changes and offers go out.

116
00:06:28.933 --> 00:06:33.025
Under the hood,
the AI has one narrow job: reading.

117
00:06:33.065 --> 00:06:35.207
Our recorded run, on this page:

118
00:06:35.247 --> 00:06:39.833
72 of 79 agreed readings
right on unseen mail.

119
00:06:39.873 --> 00:06:43.793
Run live on November 22: 275 messages,

120
00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:48.967
about $1.16, no failed calls,
73 of 81 right.

121
00:06:49.007 --> 00:06:53.263
Good, but not good enough to file alone,
so a person decides.

122
00:06:54.381 --> 00:06:58.034
Agents use the desk the way people do:
every page has an address,

123
00:06:58.074 --> 00:07:00.961
nine tasks are written out step by step,

124
00:07:01.001 --> 00:07:04.770
and a read-only browser
API returns the same data.

125
00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.891
An agent can read and propose,
but never send or move a date.

126
00:07:10.547 --> 00:07:13.687
The firm keeps its own tools: mail, files,

127
00:07:13.727 --> 00:07:17.100
calendars, texts,
e-signature, case system.

128
00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:20.077
None is connected here; six are simulated.

129
00:07:20.117 --> 00:07:23.399
A text comes in:
Maya's YES is filed by the rule;

130
00:07:23.439 --> 00:07:28.117
Leo's YES 1 3 goes to a person,
since he took only part of a docket.

131
00:07:28.803 --> 00:07:31.070
The stack is small on purpose.

132
00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.906
The record is a spreadsheet
the firm already knows;

133
00:07:33.946 --> 00:07:36.423
an outside tester rebuilt
its rules and matched

134
00:07:36.463 --> 00:07:42.383
an earlier build on all 893,010 cells
compared, in LibreOffice.

135
00:07:42.423 --> 00:07:45.483
The app is one offline React file,

136
00:07:45.523 --> 00:07:48.453
and a local server calls
the readers and holds the key.

137
00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.882
Five measures steer the firm.

138
00:07:50.922 --> 00:07:55.642
Close hearings with no yes:
four today, target zero.

139
00:07:55.682 --> 00:08:00.554
Ready three working days ahead:
18 percent, aiming for 90.

140
00:08:00.594 --> 00:08:05.742
Hearings per consultant-day:
1.7, aiming for 2.4.

141
00:08:05.782 --> 00:08:09.830
Estimated: about 92 hearings
per coordinator in a peak week,

142
00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:14.064
and $104 a hearing. The guardrail:

143
00:08:14.104 --> 00:08:18.400
results by format and consultant
must not fall as days get fuller.

144
00:08:19.026 --> 00:08:23.412
Growth means new counties,
and a new county is data, not code.

145
00:08:23.452 --> 00:08:28.421
Paste how its office works,
check what word matching read, approve.

146
00:08:28.461 --> 00:08:31.072
Kestrel Bay joins
with the same five checks.

147
00:08:32.914 --> 00:08:37.030
In simulated runs of up to 3,200 hearings,

148
00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:41.534
the tower keeps a person's time
near six minutes a hearing.

149
00:08:41.574 --> 00:08:45.404
By hand, in the same simulation,
it's about 37;

150
00:08:45.444 --> 00:08:49.021
with our measured reading errors,
under 15.

151
00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:54.379
No safety rule broke
in 45,300 simulated hearings.

152
00:08:54.419 --> 00:08:57.068
Coordinators per thousand
peak-week hearings:

153
00:08:57.108 --> 00:09:01.024
about 11 today,
5 with the tower, estimated.

154
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.139
The business case, in estimates.

155
00:09:04.179 --> 00:09:07.953
A hearing costs about $104 today.

156
00:09:07.993 --> 00:09:13.195
The weakest number is what each hearing
earns, so pin that down first.

157
00:09:13.235 --> 00:09:16.283
Season one is about $12,000 to set up,

158
00:09:16.323 --> 00:09:19.163
no new software beyond a reply rule.

159
00:09:19.203 --> 00:09:20.760
Today's coordinators run it,

160
00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:24.788
and about $10,000 of payroll
covers four counted weeks.

161
00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:29.060
A lean control tower
costs $40,000 to $70,000 a year,

162
00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.800
and pays for itself only above roughly

163
00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.574
five to nine thousand hearings a year.

164
00:09:34.614 --> 00:09:37.971
The firm handles
about 300, so the tower waits.

165
00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:42.044
Plainly:
nothing is connected to real systems yet,

166
00:09:42.084 --> 00:09:44.664
the reader tests are small and fictional,

167
00:09:44.704 --> 00:09:47.104
and every minute and dollar stays an

168
00:09:47.144 --> 00:09:49.354
estimate until the firm's work is timed.

169
00:09:49.633 --> 00:09:52.135
So the answer comes in three steps.

170
00:09:52.175 --> 00:09:56.625
First, this season:
the week-one kit in all ten counties,

171
00:09:56.665 --> 00:09:59.716
with five checks a hearing,
two daily passes,

172
00:09:59.756 --> 00:10:01.823
and whole dockets in one text.

173
00:10:02.432 --> 00:10:04.853
Next, fuller consultant-days:

174
00:10:04.893 --> 00:10:08.807
whole video days at a day rate
when a consultant chooses,

175
00:10:08.847 --> 00:10:12.336
and offices asked
for one day for our cases.

176
00:10:12.376 --> 00:10:17.065
Later, only if the firm's numbers
say it pays, the control tower.

177
00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:21.629
Either way, the next time
an office moves 9 Orchard Road,

178
00:10:21.669 --> 00:10:23.506
it's on the next morning's pass,

179
00:10:23.546 --> 00:10:26.280
and a named consultant
is there on the new day.
